   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 831 of the laws of 1981, amending the labor law\nrelating to fees and expenses in unemployment insurance proceedings, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S10567",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10567-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 831 of 1981",
    "lawSection": "Labor",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10567\n\nSPONSOR: RAMOS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 831 of the laws of 1981, amending the labor law\nrelating to fees and expenses in unemployment insurance proceedings, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend for two years provisions in Labor\nLaw that relate to fees and expenses for unemployment insurance\nproceedings.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill would extend provisions in section 538 of Labor\nLaw that relate to fees and expenses for unemployment insurance\nproceedings until December 31, 2028. These provisions direct the Unem-\nployment Insurance Appeal Board to establish qualifications and proce-\ndures for the registration of agents to represent claimants and require\nthe UIAB to maintain lists of these agents for such claimants upon\nrequest. In addition, agents seeking authorization are required to post\na $500 bond for the benefit of claimants charged certain fees by the\nAgent.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 831 of the Laws of 1981, which has been extended every two years\nsince, ensures that claimants are properly represented and not charged\nunfair fees. Extending these provisions regarding the registration proc-\ness allows claimants access to qualified agents.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter 250 of the Laws of 2024 (A.9770/S.9368)\n\nChapter 432 of the Laws of 2022 (A. 10197/S.9337)\n\nChapter 58 of the Laws of 2020 (A.9508-B/S.7508-B)\n\nChapter 257 of the Laws of 2018 (A.11026/S.8653)\n\nChapter 135 of the Laws of 2016 (A.9766/S.7854)\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act would take effect immediately.\n",
